{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;!--[if !supportLists]--&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:Arial&quot;&gt;1.&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--[endif]--&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;Flat 2\r\ndue to the low floor to ceiling height would have an unacceptable floor to ceiling\r\nheight within the loft space. Furthermore, the double bedroom within the loft\r\nspace would not have a window resulting in oppressive and cramped living\r\naccommodation. Flat 2 would provide a poor standard of living accommodation for\r\nthe future occupiers of this flat, contrary to the high quality design\r\naspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policy D6 of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021), core policy CS1.K of the Harrow Core strategy (2012),\r\npolicy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and\r\nthe adopted Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning Document (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%;\r\nfont-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The applicant has not demonstrated to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority that there would be sufficient space within the curtilage of the site to provide sufficient, convenient refuse storage for the existing and proposed flats. The proposal is therefore contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), CS1.B of the Core Strategy (2012) and policies DM1 and DM45 of The Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
